RF.put("questb:b58",{"8698":{"id":8698,"t":"Ring of the Gathering Storm","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Qiraji Magisterial Ring, 2 Vermillion Idols, 5 Silver Scarabs and 5 Bone Scarabs to Windcaller Yessendra in Silithus. You must also attain Honored reputation with Cenarion Circle to complete this quest.\nQiraji Magisterial Ring Ayamiss the Hunter 30 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Ossirian the Unscarred 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Moam 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , General Rajaxx 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 2 more\n2 Vermillion Idol Flesh Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Drone 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Collector 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Soldier 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 4 more\n5 Silver Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Bone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 9000 reputation with Cenarion Circle","desc":"The rings worn by the Qiraji lieutenants are rumored to grant them formidable abilities. The corrupted gems that adorn them could, in theory, be swapped out with more pure materials to create uncorrupted versions of the rings.\nThe gems that adorn Qiraji idols would work quite well, as their quality is superior.\nBring me the ring and idols and I'll create a powerful ring for you, ‹class›.","rew":"You will receive:\nRing of the Gathering Storm\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Did you bring me the ring and materials, ‹name›?","done":"I will swap the gem on the ring for you. You'll find the effect is much more... agreeable.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":52,"y":38.2,"n":"Windcaller Yessendra","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"79098":{"id":79098,"t":"Clear the forest","lv":60,"min":18,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Silverwing Sentinel Charm to Kazragore, Far Seer, at the Bonfire base in Ashenvale.\nProvided: Silverwing Sentinel Charm","desc":"This one is slain, but these infuriating alliance continue to fight... what is this charm?","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211816\n+1,000 reputation with Warsong Outriders\n0 reputation with Stormwind\n0 reputation with Darnassus","back":"‹name›, what news do you have from the front?","done":"These Alliance dogs still prevent us from harvesting the resources needed for Orgrimmar. Continue to drive them out!\nThis Warsong battle drum will inspire you to fight them with greater determination. Lok'tar Ogar, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":39.2,"y":67.8,"n":"Kazragore","e":1},{"z":"Ashenvale","x":74,"y":60.6,"n":"Kazragore","e":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"778":{"id":778,"t":"This Is Going to Be Hard","lv":45,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Defeat the Fam'retor Guardian and bring Lotwil's Shackles of Elemental Binding back to Lotwil Veriatus.\nLotwil's Shackles of Elemental Binding Fam'retor Guardian","desc":"Haha! Done! The shackles are done!\nIt's time, Lucien. It's time, Servo!\nAre you ready to bear witness to the perfect blend of alchemy, engineering, and the arcane, ‹name›?\nI shall summon forth a powerful elemental now. This is a groundbreaking day for all of us.","rew":"You will receive:\nNifty Stopwatch\nExperience: 4,850","back":"Not quite the outcome I was expecting. Could you get my shackles back?","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. That was quite an ordeal, wasn't it?\nI'm not sure what could have gone wrong. It was a good thing my magics were here to help send the creature back to its home plane.\nPerhaps a little token of appreciation for all your hard work...","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":25.9,"y":44.9,"n":"Lotwil Veriatus","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"1578":{"id":1578,"t":"Supplying the Front","lv":12,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 6 Copper Axes and 6 Copper Chain Belts to Thorvald in the southern guard tower of Loch Modan.\n6 Copper Axe\n6 Copper Chain Belt","desc":"The mountaineers of Loch Modan are fighting troggs, and having a busy time of it! They need constant supplies of new armor and weapons if we're ever to get a handle on those troggs.\nThat's why my colleague Thorvald is there, trying to keep the mountaineers in good gear. So if you were to make some copper axes and copper chain belts and bring them to Thorvald, he would be obliged. He might even share his knowledge with you.\nThorvald is in Loch Modan's southern guard tower.","rew":"You will receive:\nPlans: Copper Chain Vest\nExperience: 900\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"I have no time to chat. Do you have business with me?","done":"Ah, apologies! I didn't realize you were here to help resupply our troops. The stuff you made will be a big help!\nHere are plans for some armor. I hope you find them useful.\nDun Morogh Loch Modan","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.9,"y":27.9,"n":"Tormus Deepforge","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":23.7,"y":74.3,"n":"Thorvald Deepforge","e":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"7658":{"id":7658,"t":"Imperial Plate Leggings","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"60 Thorium Bar","rew":"You will receive:\nPlans: Imperial Plate Leggings\n+200 reputation with Thorium Brotherhood","back":"Just hand over 60 thorium bars and the leg plans are yers.\nI know, I'm driving you into bankruptcy! I've heard it all before so you can save your sob story, weakling.","done":"A pleasure doin' business with ya.\nAnd ‹name›, wipe that look of disgust off yer face.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":51.4,"y":28.7,"n":"Derotain Mudsipper","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"96058":{"id":96058,"t":"Camping 101 engineering","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Bronk Guzzlegear in Kharanos to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your engineering skill to 20","desc":"Engineers like yourself can cook up all sorts of bits, bots, and bombs for fun and profit.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Reagent Bot for your camp. This helpful automaton can help keep you well-supplied so that you and your allies never run out of the materials needed to fuel your spells.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Reagent Bot. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":46.6,"y":53.8,"n":"Eric Brighthammer","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":50.2,"y":50.4,"n":"Bronk Guzzlegear","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"92458":{"id":92458,"t":"Heart of disruption","lv":33,"min":24,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect the Arcane Mote for the Image of Archmage Modera near the City of Dalaran.\nArcane Mote","desc":"Whatever disturbed the ley lines, it started at the top of the Violet Citadel. A thunderous crash rang out from the parlors above, and now we are overrun with rampant arcane power. It's taking all we have just to keep the wards in place.\nWe cannot afford to stall any longer. We need help.\nThe Kirin Tor are busy inside, but you will still need a less public approach to gain entry. Take this key and meet me in the citadel once you've made your way into the city. We must put an end to this disruption.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSpellguard Pauldrons Renewing Footpads Defender of Dalaran\nExperience: 9,400\n+100 reputation with Kirin Tor\nLevel 33 , requires level 24 Difficulty 24 29 31 36 42 Side Alliance Type Dungeon Quest ID 92458\nThe chain\n3 quests at level 33, 10,320 XP in all.\n1 [ 33 ] An Alarming Request\nReport to the Image of Archmage Modera near the City of Dalaran.\nEmissary Jacques Hillsbrad Foothills\n650 XP\n2 [ 33 ] Heart of Disruption this quest\nCollect the Arcane Mote for the Image of Archmage Modera near the City of Dalaran.\n9,400 XP\n3 [ 33 ] Friend of the Kirin Tor\nSpeak to Archmage Celindra in the City of Dalaran.\n270 XP","cats":["city-of-dalaran"]},"94218":{"id":94218,"t":"Craftsmans writ elixir of defense","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Elixir of Defense\nElixir of Defense","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Elixir of Defense, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Elixir of Defense Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94218","cats":["crafting"]},"94298":{"id":94298,"t":"Craftsmans writ swift boots","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Swift Boots\nSwift Boots","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Swift Boots, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Swift Boots Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94298","cats":["crafting"]},"7898":{"id":7898,"t":"Thorium Widget","lv":60,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"6 Thorium Widget Wildspawn Shadowstalker 0 % , Gordok Warlock 0 % , Thuzadin Shadowcaster 0 % in Stratholme , Blackhand Iron Guard 0 % and 2 more","rew":"You will receive:\n20 Darkmoon Faire Prize Ticket\n+100 reputation with Darkmoon Faire","back":"Yebb Nebblegear, like me, is working on a future attraction. So amazing is this attraction, says Nebb, that it will draw folks from across the world... and it will make us all very, very rich!\nHe says he needs thorium widgets for its construction, and wants me to collect them for him. So what do you say, ‹name›? Do you know where to get Thorium widgets? If you're an engineer, can you make them? Do you want to trade them for Darkmoon Faire tickets?","done":"Ah, thank you, ‹name›! Yebb will enjoy these widgets. I don't know what he has planned for them, but Yebb's a clever little gnome. He's clever, and maybe a little devious....\nIf only he liked the taste of humanoid flesh... he'd make a great troll!\nHere, ‹name›. A deal's a deal, and these tickets are yours.\nMulgore Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":38,"y":44.3,"n":"Rinling","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":41.7,"y":70.7,"n":"Rinling","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"2138":{"id":2138,"t":"Cleansing of the Infected","lv":16,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Cleanse the forest of 20 Rabid Thistle Bears and return to Tharnariun Treetender in Darkshore.\nRabid Thistle Bear slain : 0/ 20","desc":"As I had feared, the cure does not work.\nIt saddens me greatly to order the death of any of nature's beasts, but the sick and tainted thistle bears must be put down.\nReturn to the forest and destroy 20 rabid thistle bears, ‹name›. It will most certainly not put a stop to the plague but it will slow down the damage the animals are doing to our forest and its inhabitants for a short time.","rew":"Experience: 1,150\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Is your task complete?","done":"You have done Auberdine a great service, ‹name›, but your task is not yet complete.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":38.8,"y":43.4,"n":"Tharnariun Treetender","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"7498":{"id":7498,"t":"Garona: A Study on Stealth and Treachery","lv":60,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 7,050, 0.94 times as much.","obj":"Return the book to its rightful owners.\nGarona: A Study on Stealth and Treachery A Dusty Tome 0 % , A Dusty Tome 0 %\nProvided: Garona: A Study on Stealth and Treachery","desc":"The tome carries the mark of the Athenaeum.","rew":"You will receive:\nRoyal Seal of Eldre'Thalas\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Shen'dralar","back":"You have recovered a tome!","done":"Excellent work, ‹race›. Should you find any more tomes, do not hesitate to return them to us.\nAs time passes, we tend to change around and even add new rewards for the return of missing tomes.\nStart an item: Garona: A Study on Stealth and Treachery End Lorekeeper Kildrath Level 60 , requires level 54 Difficulty 54 56 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Class Rogue Type Dungeon Shareable No Quest ID 7498","cats":["dire-maul"]},"218":{"id":218,"t":"The Stolen Journal","lv":5,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Grelin Whitebeard wants you to kill Grik'nir the Cold, and retrieve his journal.\nGrelin Whitebeard's Journal Grik'nir the Cold","desc":"My journal! They took it away to the cave. The one that had it... It was a big brute with some odd markings on his skin and face. I didn't get a much better look than that.\nYou've had some luck with the trolls, maybe you could go get it back for me?","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDwarven Kite Shield Smooth Walking Staff\nExperience: 550\n+150 reputation with Ironforge\n+200 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"‹name›! Any luck?","done":"Wonderful, ‹name›! Many thanks for retrieving my notebook. Well, it would seem that the troll situation here in Coldridge Valley is under control and not much cause for worry.\nAfter I put the finishing touches on my report, I'll need someone to courier it to my brother Senir.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":25.1,"y":75.7,"n":"Grelin Whitebeard","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"96138":{"id":96138,"t":"Merricks bow","lv":28,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Defeat 8 Splint Fist Warriors and 4 Splint Fist Taskmasters then return to Sirra Von'Indi in Darkshire for more information.\nSplinter Fist Warrior slain : 0/ 8\nSplinter Fist Taskmaster slain : 0/ 4\nProvided: Merrick's Bow","desc":"A bow left by the spirit of Merrick Valor, famed Watcher who prided himself on keeping the roads safe from encroaching enemies.\nWith Merrick's spirit still wandering the roads, perhaps his unfinished business was to clear out invaders near his home in Raven Hill. The ogres south of town may be what's troubling his spirit.\nDuskwood Open the zone on the world map Start an item: Merrick's Bow Level 28 , requires level 18 Difficulty 18 24 26 31 36 Side Alliance Quest ID 96138","cats":["duskwood"]},"58":{"id":58,"t":"The Night Watch","lv":30,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Commander Althea Ebonlocke of Darkshire wants you to kill 20 Plague Spreaders in the eastern Raven Hill mausoleum.\nPlague Spreader slain : 0/ 20","desc":"The situation in Raven Hill is still grim. The safety of Darkshire is in your hands, ‹name›. I don't have enough Watchers to keep the town safe. We need you to dispatch for Raven Hill yet again and rid the eastern mausoleum of 20 Plague Spreaders!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBandolier of the Night Watch Quiver of the Night Watch Gunnysack of the Night Watch\nMoney: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,450\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"I need your assistance, ‹name›. Travel to the cemetery to the northwest and rid the eastern mausoleum of 20 Plague Spreaders.\nReturn to me when your task is complete.","done":"On behalf of the people of Darkshire and as the Leader of the Night Watch, I thank you, ‹name›, for your bravery and dedication. May the Light shine upon your ways.","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":73.5,"y":46.8,"n":"Commander Althea Ebonlocke","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"1258":{"id":1258,"t":"... and Bugs","lv":40,"min":33,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 12 Pristine Crawler Legs to Morgan Stern in Theramore.\n12 Pristine Crawler Leg Monstrous Crawler 80 % , Silt Crawler 80 %","desc":"Another component of my new recipe is the shelled leg of a giant crab. And the crabs they have in Dustwallow -- Muckshells they call them -- just won't do! I'm afraid the only suitable crabs live far away, in the Swamp of Sorrows.\nThe shell of the crab leg is a key element of the dish's presentation so I need pristine, unscarred legs. An adult crab might only have one or two such legs, and I need a lot in order to research my dish.\nSo, ‹name›... are you willing to travel?","rew":"You will receive:\nBaroque Apron\nExperience: 3,150\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"My research with the Mudrock tongues is progressing nicely. I trust your crab hunt goes well?","done":"These are wonderful specimens, ‹name›! The shells are in perfect condition, and the meat is pink and tender. The blood of a chef is in your veins, I'm sure of it!\nDustwallow Marsh Swamp of Sorrows","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":66.3,"y":45.5,"n":"Morgan Stern","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"9178":{"id":9178,"t":"Craftsman's Writ - Dense Weightstone","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver 120 Dense Weightstones and the Craftsman's Writ - Dense Weightstone - to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nCraftsman's Writ - Dense Weightstone\n120 Dense Weightstone\nProvided: Craftsman's Writ - Dense Weightstone","desc":"The bearer of this writ is entitled to payment in the form of an insignia of their choice upon completion of the contracted work order.\nWork Order BS-091:\n120 Dense Weightstones.\nAll filled orders should be delivered to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nContract is null and void if tampered with or damaged.\n-Dispatch Commander Metz, The Argent Dawn","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nInsignia of the Crusade Insignia of the Dawn\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Filling a work order, ‹class›?","done":"Yep, these will come in handy for the infantry's bashin' weapons.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":70.7,"y":48.5,"n":"Packmaster Stonebruiser","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"91738":{"id":91738,"t":"An apple treat","lv":10,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Thunder Applejack","rew":"Money: 2 50 0 gold, 2 silver, 50 copper Experience: 625","back":"The sergeant's eyes light up as he notices your bottle of Thunder Applejack...\nThunder Applejack (1)","done":"Do my eyes deceive me? I haven't seen a drop of Thunder Applejack in months!\nThis should put a smile on the troops' faces. You have my thanks, ‹class›!","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":24,"y":73,"n":"Sergeant De Vries","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"4298":{"id":4298,"t":"Becoming a Parent","lv":48,"min":38,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Agnar Beastamer in the Hinterlands.","desc":"Whoa, it was a lot more ready than I thought...","rew":"You will receive:\nSprite Darter Egg\nExperience: 440\n+25 reputation with Darnassus\n+25 reputation with Wildhammer Clan","done":"Here, take the egg... better you have it so it bonds to you and looks to you to be its dadda/momma.\nCongrats, ‹name›. You're a parent... kinda.","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":14.2,"y":43.6,"n":"Agnar Beastamer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"7738":{"id":7738,"t":"Perfect Yeti Hide","lv":48,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 440 experience instead of 2,200, 0.2 times as much.","obj":"Bring the Perfect Yeti Hide to Jangdor Swiftstrider at Camp Mojache, Feralas.\nPerfect Yeti Hide Lurking Feral Scar 25 % , Ferocious Rage Scar 10 % , Elder Rage Scar 10 % , Rage Scar Yeti 10 %\nProvided: Perfect Yeti Hide","desc":"You have found what may very well be a perfect yeti hide. You easily note that it is exceptionally thick and sturdy - more so than even the ones you've seen from the yeti in Rage Scar.\nConsidering that Jangdor Swiftstrider at Camp Mojache is in the market for yeti hides, this particular one may be of considerable interest to him.","rew":"Money: 7 0 gold, 7 silver, 0 copper Experience: 440\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"What's this, ‹name› - you've got something special for me?","done":"This is an incredible find! I believe this is the finest yeti hide specimen I have ever seen!\nIndeed, this is certainly worthy of an appropriate bounty. I normally don't pay that much for a single hide, but I'm confident I can make something special from it. Thanks for thinking of me on this, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":74.4,"y":42.9,"n":"Jangdor Swiftstrider","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"2858":{"id":2858,"t":"Wild Leather Boots","lv":45,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 45 instead of 48.","obj":"Bring 2 Nightscape Pants, 2 Nightscape Boots, and 2 Wildvines to Jangdor Swiftstrider in Camp Mojache.\n2 Nightscape Pants\n2 Nightscape Boots\n2 Wildvine Retherokk the Berserker 80.6 % , Zul'arek Hatefowler 65.1 % , Purple Lotus 10 % , Vilebranch Aman'zasi Guard 9.5 % and 4 more","desc":"Your knowledge of Wild Leather armor grows, ‹name›; still, there is more for you to learn.\nWild Leather boots are the cornerstone of any set. Such boots are crafted to cradle the foot in comfort while bracing it against the hazards of adventuring. The soft soles are a blessing to those seeking quiet movement in footwear.\nFor this pattern, I need two Nightscape pants and two Nightscape boots crafted. I also will require two wildvines... not just one. When you have these items, we will proceed.","rew":"You will receive:\nPattern: Wild Leather Boots\nExperience: 2,900","back":"The pants, boots, and wildvines need to be delivered to me before you learn the pattern, ‹name›. Have you done as I asked?\nFrom the earliest pair of boots we learn how to make, we start to understand that a quality boot needs to ride a razor's edge between comfort and function. With both, we are able to create items that allow the wearer to ignore fatigue that would cripple those wearing lower quality goods.","done":"Once again, you have produced items with the skill of a seasoned professional. You have earned this pattern, as well as my congratulations.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":74.4,"y":42.9,"n":"Jangdor Swiftstrider","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["leatherworking"]},"1338":{"id":1338,"t":"Stormpike's Order","lv":14,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Stormpike's Request to Furen Longbeard in Stormwind.\nStormpike's Request\nProvided: Stormpike's Request","desc":"There is a dwarven armorsmith whose work I admire greatly. His name is Furen Longbeard, and his skill is unmatched. I need a new shield, and I must have one of his!\nThe problem is... Furen is far to the south, in the dwarven district within Stormwind. In human lands! I can't imagine why he would live there, so far from Ironforge. The humans must pay him a king's ransom to keep him there!\nSo, if you want to travel and don't mind making some money, then will you send Furen my request for a shield?","rew":"Money: 6 0 gold, 6 silver, 0 copper Experience: 975\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"A letter from the dwarven lands? I wonder who would call from so far to the north...\nPlease, let me see the order.","done":"Ah, a request from one of the Stormpikes. That's a proud clan, full of quality dwarves. Rich ones, too.\nThank you, ‹name›. I'll get to work on Mountaineer Stormpike's shield by the end of the day.\nLoch Modan Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":24.8,"y":18.4,"n":"Mountaineer Stormpike","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":64.6,"y":37.2,"n":"Furen Longbeard","e":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"298":{"id":298,"t":"Excavation Progress Report","lv":15,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Ironband's Progress Report to Jern Hornhelm in Thelsamar.\nIronband's Progress Report\nProvided: Ironband's Progress Report","desc":"I need a progress report sent to Thelsamar - a progress report, and a restatement of my request for more blastpowder! Here's the report. Take it to Jern Hornhelm. He's our local contact in Thelsamar.\nIt's not a difficult task, but it must be done.","rew":"Experience: 270\n+25 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Oh, a progress report from the site? Very good!","done":"Bah! Ironband's having trouble with the Troggs. I wonder if he wants that blastpowder to aid his digging, or to aid his efforts against the Trogg beasts...\nWell, either way it's powder well spent!\nBut what's strange is, I sent him plenty of blastpowder weeks ago. I wonder where it went...","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":65.9,"y":65.6,"n":"Prospector Ironband","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":37.2,"y":47.4,"n":"Jern Hornhelm","e":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"3098":{"id":3098,"t":"Glyphic Scroll","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Glyphic Scroll and speak to Isabella in the church in Deathknell.\nGlyphic Scroll\nProvided: Glyphic Scroll","desc":"Ah, while you were off dealing with the mindless Scourge, this scroll arrived for you. I would think it's some matter of importance as it seems it bears the seal of the mage trainer Isabella. I would take some time to read it before heading out again.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Undercity","back":"I knew you would come to me, ‹name›. Not because you do not have the will to follow your own path, but because we are kindred spirits. We both have felt pain. We have both suffered. And now we want the power to take back what we know is ours: this land, our lives, our destinies. But there is much for you to learn still.","done":"You must return to me often if you are to become powerful enough to destroy those who would oppose us. The rules of magic still apply to you, ‹name›. You will still find corruption follows you like hungry wolves in the night. You will find its caress is not unlike an addiction, an old lover still wanting to be by your side. But these things can be staved off. These things will only control you if you allow them to.\nGo now, return to me when you've grown more powerful.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":30.8,"y":66.2,"n":"Shadow Priest Sarvis","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":30.9,"y":66.1,"n":"Isabella","e":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"9098":{"id":9098,"t":"Frostfire Shoulderpads","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Archmage Angela Dosantos at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Frostfire Shoulderpads if you bring her the following: 1 Desecrated Shoulderpads, 12 Wartorn Cloth Scraps, 2 Mooncloth and 3 Cured Rugged Hides.\nDesecrated Shoulderpads Grobbulus 0 % in Naxxramas , Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Patchwerk 0 % in Naxxramas\n12 Wartorn Cloth Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 35 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 30.3 % in Naxxramas , Bile Retcher 28.5 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 28.3 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n2 Mooncloth\n3 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"As a Watcher, I was allowed access to many of Medivh's personal effects. Among those items, I found the tomes most enlightening. While the majority of the books were filled with - to put it bluntly - tripe, there were some gems. One of those tomes documented the creation of a set of armor fit for an archmage: Frostfire.\n<Angela points to her head.>\nIt's all in here and I am willing to share the fruits of that knowledge with you as long as you are able to provide me with the necessary materials.","rew":"You will receive:\nFrostfire Shoulderpads\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !,\nyou got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Frostfire Shoulderpads.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.7,"n":"Archmage Angela Dosantos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"1018":{"id":1018,"t":"The New Frontier","lv":55,"min":54,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem on the Elder Rise of Thunder Bluff about the Cenarion Circle's call to explore the frontiers of Kalimdor.","desc":"Attention, heroes!\nThe Cenarion Circle seeks able bodied individuals to assist them in exploring the vast new frontiers of Kalimdor! A forbidden wasteland of unimaginable dangers lies far to the west of Tanaris and Gadgetzan, and the Circle needs willing and honorable proxies to act in their stead.\nAll interested individuals should seek audience with the Cenarion Circle. Speak with the Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem on the Elder's Rise of Thunder Bluff for more information!","rew":"Experience: 550\n+10 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"Greetings, ‹class›.\nI am pleased to see the likes of you taking an interest in the well being of nature; tales of your mighty deeds precede you, and you are welcomed here. Seeing you before me instills the feeling of confidence that the Cenarion Circle will get the proper aid it needs.\nOur connection with the Cenarion Circle in Moonglade transcends racial and political divides. Remember this as you work on behalf of the Circle, and you will do well.\nOrgrimmar Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":48.2,"y":66.1,"n":"Warcaller Gorlach","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":78.6,"y":28.6,"n":"Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"9018":{"id":9018,"t":"Anthion's Parting Words","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Mokvar in Orgimmar with a set of Magister's Boots, Magister's Leggings and Magister's Mantle.\nMagister's Boots Hearthsinger Forresten 0 % in Stratholme\nMagister's Leggings Baron Rivendare 0 % in Stratholme\nMagister's Mantle\nProvided: Banner of Provocation","desc":"Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet. In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.\nThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the amulet back together. Return to Mokvar and tell him that Bodley is his only hope for finding the remaining pieces. Speak to him about any rewards you've arranged for.\nI, for once, shall rest in peace. I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!","rew":"You will receive:\nSorcerer's Boots Sorcerer's Leggings Sorcerer's Mantle\nExperience: 9,950","back":"You've returned and I see in your eyes that you've much to tell me, ‹name›. Let us take care of your reward first.","done":"This curse was bestowed upon us but for a mere medallion. Lord Valthalak certainly knows how to hold a grudge.\nWe'll endeavor to find the remaining pieces - hopefully before I meet an untimely demise. But before that, let us see about your reward.\nEastern Plaguelands Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":26.1,"y":11.3,"n":"Anthion Harmon","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"8938":{"id":8938,"t":"Just Compensation","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Beaststalker's Belt and a set of Beaststalker's Gloves to Mokvar in Orgrimmar.\nBeaststalker's Belt Smolderthorn Headhunter 4.2 % , Rage Talon Dragon Guard 3.8 % , Firebrand Legionnaire 3.1 % , Bloodaxe Raider 2.7 % and 2 more\nBeaststalker's Gloves War Master Voone 0 %","desc":"You've proven to be a very reliable individual, ‹name›. As much as I trust that you'll help me through this predicament, it would be wise of me to reward you according to your performance.\nFor now I will exchange your belt and gloves. If we both see this through I shall make the rest of the pieces available to you.","rew":"You will receive:\nBeastmaster's Belt Beastmaster's Gloves\nExperience: 9,950","back":"You're ready to perform the exchange?","done":"Our agreement remains in place. Just remember, this is but a taste of what awaits you. Free me of this cursed fate and I will reward you with items of truly great power.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"94778":{"id":94778,"t":"Divine grace","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak to High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind.","desc":"You're needed in Stormwind, ‹name›. The High Priestess there, Laurena, says it's time for you to prove you're worthy of the next level of your training. Don't waste too much time finding your way there. You can find her in the Cathedral of Light in the center of the city. Give her my regards, and prove how worthy you are of such a calling. The Light be with you, ‹name›.\nLevel 10 , requires level 10 Difficulty 10 13 16 Side Alliance Class Priest Shareable Yes Quest ID 94778","cats":["priest"]},"5658":{"id":5658,"t":"Touch of Weakness","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Aelthalyste in the Undercity.","desc":"You be far from home, ‹class›. You be needed there, back in your city under the ground. Your mistress, the one you be callin' Aelthalyste be needin' you back there. Like my tribe, there things you must learn only from her. Don't be stayin' here too long. You should be headin' to the War Quarter as fast as a zeppelin can carry you.","rew":"You will learn: Touch of Weakness","done":"Ah, young ‹class›, I am glad you have returned here. I would teach you a lesson you would do well to not forget. Are you prepared?","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":49.1,"y":14.6,"n":"Father Lankester","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":49.3,"y":17.1,"n":"Aelthalyste","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"2218":{"id":2218,"t":"Road to Salvation","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Hulfdan Blackbeard in Ironforge.","desc":"Another lost soul looking for guidance, eh? I suppose you want to find a purpose - your purpose. I've seen it a thousand times, another hero looking for work.\nWell, today's your lucky day, friend. Hogral's got the cure for your ailment.\nHere's what you do: Take this road here up to Ironforge and make your way to the Forlorn Cavern. Once there, locate the thieves' guild and speak with Hulfdan Blackbeard. He'll put you on the road to salvation.","rew":"Money: 1 75 0 gold, 1 silver, 75 copper Experience: 420","done":"So ye think yer a right scoundrel? Destined to be one o' Blackbeard's chosen few - an officer o' the Hidden Circle?\nOnly a good fer nothin' scallywag would think so highly o' hisself.\nThat's exactly what we be lookin' fer! Welcome aboard, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":47.6,"y":52.6,"n":"Hogral Bakkan","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":59.4,"y":23.5,"n":"Hulfdan Blackbeard","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"1898":{"id":1898,"t":"The Deathstalkers","lv":13,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Andron Gant in the Undercity.\nAstor's Letter of Introduction Astor Hadren\nProvided: Astor's Letter of Introduction","desc":"The letter of introduction should be enough to convince Andron that you are the messenger he's been waiting for. I've met Andron before, he doesn't quite have the mental capacity to be that suspicious.\nLord Varimathras suspects that Andron has been providing aid to some other group. He wishes to know what organization this is and requires proof of it.\nI want you to speak with Andron, and obtain this information. You'll find him at his shop near the Apothecarium.","rew":"Experience: 230","back":"Hello. Something I can do for you?","done":"Ah, yes, I've been expecting you. I have no doubt our mutual acquaintances are pleased with the information that I have provided so far?\nI suppose there's no point in asking you, I doubt they would burden you with this knowledge. Why place so much trust in the messenger, hm?","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":83.5,"y":69.1,"n":"Mennet Carkad","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":54.8,"y":76.3,"n":"Andron Gant","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"1978":{"id":1978,"t":"The Deathstalkers","lv":13,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver Andron's Ledger to Varimathras in the Hall of the Dark Lady in the Undercity.\nAndron's Ledger Andron's Bookshelf\nProvided: Andron's Ledger","desc":"The Syndicate? I would never have suspected. It seems the lords of Alterac have fallen far in the years since their betrayal.\nLord Varimathras will be pleased to learn of this, and as you were so instrumental in this discovery, it would be fitting if you were the one to deliver it to him.\nAh, and how could I forget?\nWelcome to the Deathstalkers.","rew":"You will receive:\nBlade of Cunning\nExperience: 900","back":"Yes?","done":"Hmm, this is interesting. The Deathstalkers have performed their duties admirably in ferreting this out.\nFrom what I understand, you also deserve commendation for your performance. I hope that this will become routine for you, ‹name›, my Deathstalkers always have use of a good man.\nUndercity Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":83.5,"y":69.1,"n":"Mennet Carkad","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":56.3,"y":92.2,"n":"Varimathras","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"2378":{"id":2378,"t":"Find the Shattered Hand","lv":16,"min":16,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Journey to Orgrimmar and speak with Shenthul at the Cleft of Shadow.","desc":"You have served the Deathstalkers well, ‹name›, but perhaps it is time for you to venture outward. While you have shown aptitude in the ways of stealth and deception, you still require much training.\nThe Deathstalkers have allies within the Shattered Hand. Seek out those that would assist us - find Shenthul in Orgrimmar.","rew":"Experience: 120","done":"So, you are what our mighty allies have sent Shenthul? How uninspiring....\nUndercity Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":83.5,"y":69.1,"n":"Mennet Carkad","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":43,"y":53.7,"n":"Shenthul","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"2298":{"id":2298,"t":"Kingly Shakedown","lv":16,"min":16,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Stormwind and seek out Renzik \"The Shiv.\"","desc":"So there we were, about to start plottin' out phase III when a couple o' Magni's blockheads come bargin' in here talkin' bout some kind o' heist and arresting some o' the Hidden Circle.\nWell nobody puts the iron on old Blackbeard! The argumentations got heavy and thick and somehow yer name weres blurted out!\nMe advice? Take the first Gryphon out o' Ironforge and get to Stormwind. Get yerself to Old Town and once there, talk to an old friend o' mine named Renzik \"The Shiv.\"","rew":"Experience: 120","done":"It's always good to have one of Hulfdan's rogues among our ranks!\nDun Morogh Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":59.4,"y":23.5,"n":"Hulfdan Blackbeard","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":78.3,"y":71.1,"n":"Renzik \"The Shiv\"","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"2458":{"id":2458,"t":"Deep Cover","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to the Venture Co. Tower, north of the Sludge Fen and contact the Shattered Hand's covert operative, Taskmaster Fizzule.\nWhen the tower is in sight, use the Flare Gun to signal your arrival to Taskmaster Fizzule. Fire off TWO flares, then approach Taskmaster Fizzule and perform the Shattered /Salute.\nThese actions must be performed in the correct order, as Fizzule will attack and terminate any person he does not recognize.\nProvided: Flare Gun","desc":"The Venture Company... Perhaps you have heard of them?\nFor one year we have worked on planting an agent deep within their ranks. Through much hard work and careful planning, we succeeded.\nRecently we received word that the Venture Co. are planning something on a grand scale. Go north of the Sludge Fen to the Venture Co. tower and contact our undercover agent, Taskmaster Fizzule.\nWhen you find the tower, use this flare gun, then approach Fizzule and show him the salute of the Shattered Hand.","rew":"You will receive:\nFizzule's Whistle\nExperience: 1,150","done":"It's good to see another agent of the Shattered Hand in these parts, however, the flare may have been a little too much!\nNext time you need to speak with me, blow into this whistle twice and I'll know you are an ally.\nOrgrimmar The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":43,"y":53.7,"n":"Shenthul","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":55.4,"y":5.6,"n":"Taskmaster Fizzule","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"1658":{"id":1658,"t":"Crashing the Wickerman Festival (PvP)","lv":60,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from Crashing the Wickerman Festival (PvP). Pays 90s instead of 0.","obj":"Locate the Forsaken's Wickerman Festival in Tirisfal Glade. Return to Sergeant Hartman in Southshore once you've done so.\nFind the place the quest sends you to.","desc":"I need brave individuals to head up to Tirisfal Glade and check out the Wickerman Festival. I'm not going to lie - heading up there will be dangerous. The guards at the festival will be exceptionally vicious. Still, we need to know how big the festival is this year, and how much trouble the Forsaken are going to cause us during Hallow's End.\nIf you're up for it, head to Tirisfal and scout out the festival. Return to me with the information, and I'll make sure you're well compensated.","rew":"You will receive:\n15 Hallow's End Pumpkin Treat\nMoney: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Alliance","done":"Well done, ‹name›. The Wickerman Festival will continue to be trouble so long as the abominable Forsaken are allowed to haunt the remnants of Lordaeron. It is NOT a fitting tribute to that once proud kingdom, let me tell you...\nHere's some coin for any repairs you might need, and in the spirit of the season I've also included some treats you might like. Happy Hallow's End - let's keep it as safe as possible here in Southshore.\nHillsbrad Foothills Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":50,"y":57.5,"n":"Sergeant Hartman","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"1098":{"id":1098,"t":"Deathstalkers in Shadowfang","lv":25,"min":18,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 5,350 experience instead of 2,000, 2.68 times as much. New rewards: Tanned Shoulderpads, Bronzed Shoulderguards. Read from what the game server sent.","obj":"Find the Deathstalker Adamant and Deathstalker Vincent.","desc":"In preparation for an assault on Shadowfang, two deathstalkers were sent to the keep to gather intelligence. It has been many days and they have not returned, but we must receive their report if we're to have any hope of a successful attack!\nSo here is your task, ‹name›. Go to Shadowfang Keep to the south and find the Deathstalkers Adamant and Vincent. Find them, and if they require aid then give it.\nThis mission is as dangerous as is it critical, ‹name›. Do not fail.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGhostly Mantle Tanned Shoulderpads Bronzed Shoulderguards\nNew in Forever: Tanned Shoulderpads, Bronzed Shoulderguards.\nMoney: 18 0 gold, 18 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,350\n+100 reputation with Undercity","done":"Vincent's body lies broken, and still.\nAlthough Deathstalker Adamant will send his report to Hadrec... whatever additional details Vincent gained must remain with him.\nBut clutched in his hand is a small trinket...","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":43.4,"y":40.9,"n":"High Executor Hadrec","s":1}],"cats":["shadowfang-keep"]},"9338":{"id":9338,"t":"Allegiance to Cenarion Circle","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Cenarion Combat Badge\nCenarion Logistics Badge\nCenarion Tactical Badge","back":"Even if you have no need for the material rewards we offer, these badges still mark our mutual trust and friendship.\nBring them to me. I'll make due note of your service should your performance go above and beyond the call of duty.","done":"You honor us, ‹name›. With your continued efforts we will overcome all obstacles.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":50,"y":36.4,"n":"Windcaller Kaldon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8378":{"id":8378,"t":"Armaments of War","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Reservist's Leggings Dunestalker's Boots\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"War comes, ‹name›, and with it comes untold horrors. You have done all that could be asked of you and for that you should be rewarded.\nShould this... this prophecy ever come to pass...\n<Geologist Larksbane turns pale.>\nThe future of us all could be at an end.\nThese armaments will prove invaluable to your campaign in this desert.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.7,"y":37.5,"n":"Geologist Larksbane","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8858":{"id":8858,"t":"Secrets of the Colossus - Regal","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Colossus of Regal's Husk to Overseer Oilfist in Searing Gorge.\nColossus of Regal's Husk\nProvided: Colossus of Regal's Husk","desc":"There ain't nothin' I'd like more than to stuff this bug husk down Oilfist's fat face... Cept, I'm stuck here collectin' samples from that overgrown cockroach. I'll be here 'till the wee mornin' hours given the size o' that thing.\nTake this here sample to Oilfist fer me and do it fast, ‹class›. He's payin' BIG!\nYar, Thorium Point - it be in the Searin' Gorge.","rew":"You will receive:\nColossal Bag of Loot\nMoney: 2 70 2 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Thorium Brotherhood\n+200 reputation with Thorium Brotherhood\n+200 reputation with Thorium Brotherhood\n+200 reputation with Thorium Brotherhood","back":"Hmmm...","done":"Excellent. We could surely devise some incredibly powerful armor from this chitin. Here's the riches you were promised.\nSilithus Searing Gorge","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.6,"y":37.3,"n":"Colossus Researcher Eazel","s":1},{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":38.1,"y":27,"n":"Overseer Oilfist","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8538":{"id":8538,"t":"The Four Dukes","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find a way to summon and slay the Duke of Cynders, the Duke of Fathoms, the Duke of Zephyrs and the Duke of Shards and report back to Commander Mar'alith in Cenarion Hold. You must also bring Tactical Task Briefing V in order to complete this quest.\nTactical Task Briefing V\nThe Duke of Cynders slain\nThe Duke of Fathoms slain\nThe Duke of Zephyrs slain\nThe Duke of Shards slain\nProvided: Tactical Task Briefing V","desc":"The links between the Twilight's Hammer and the Abyssal Council are proving to be more important than we had expected.\nWe believe the elemental nobles known as the Abyssal Dukes are one of the primary force organizing the Twilight's Hammer cultists. Find a way to lure the four Abyssal Dukes into our plane of existence and destroy them!\nYour dedication and prowess in past assignments have led us to choose you for this particular assignment. We are certain you will succeed in this endeavor.","rew":"You will receive:\nMark of Cenarius\nExperience: 650\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Is your task done yet, ‹name›?","done":"You have achieved a great accomplishment for our cause today, ‹name›. You've vanquished some of our most powerful enemies. For that I greatly commend you.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.2,"y":34.2,"n":"Commander Mar'alith","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8778":{"id":8778,"t":"The Ironforge Brigade Needs Explosives!","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 6 Oils of Immolation, 5 Goblin Rocket Fuel and 10 Dense Blasting Powder to Arcanist Nozzlespring near Hive'Zora in Silithus. You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing IV in order to complete this quest.\n6 Oil of Immolation Molten Destroyer 0 % , Southsea Freebooter 0 % , Jadefire Betrayer 0 % , Bloodpetal Flayer 0 % and 2 more\n5 Goblin Rocket Fuel Stormpike Shredder Unit 19 % , 7:XT 2.3 % , Clunk 1.2 % , Tortured Druid 0 % and 2 more\n10 Dense Blasting Powder\nLogistics Task Briefing IV\nProvided: Logistics Task Briefing IV","desc":"The Ironforge Brigade has put in an unusual request for highly... volatile... components. Gather them and bring them to Mr. Nozzlespring from the Ironforge Brigade.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Logistics Badge Followup Logistics Assignment\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"You have something for me, ‹name›?","done":"Ah, yes! These will come in handy! Much obliged, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":32.5,"y":52,"n":"Arcanist Nozzlespring","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"98298":{"id":98298,"t":"Arugals folly","lv":16,"min":9,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring 6 Worgen Bits to Dalar Dawnweaver in The Sepulcher.\n6 Worgen Bits","desc":"Ah, it's all become so embarrassingly clear! Arugal hardly had any magic at all, let alone enough to create the worgen. 'Arugal's Curse.' Pah! Barely potent enough to last a few seconds.\nThese shackles prove he can bind the beasts, not create them. The worgen clearly spread their curse a different way. I would know how.\nGo to the Greymane Wall to the south. The worgen seem to be spreading to the humans nearby. Tear the beasts apart and bring me whatever you find. This requires a more direct approach.","rew":"You will receive:\nFoulfur Gloves\nMoney: 8 0 gold, 8 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,150\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Fangs, claws, gizzards. It makes no difference to me. The easiest way to study something is to see the guts yourself.","done":"It appears I get the last laugh after all, haha! Arugal truly was a fool. And I, Dalar Dawnweaver, have exposed him as the fraud he is.\nThese pieces are all the proof I need that the curse has nothing to do with that blithering dolt.\nRegrettably, that means his remedy is also worth nothing. It seems the search for a solution to the worgen curse continues.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":44.2,"y":39.8,"n":"Dalar Dawnweaver","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"538":{"id":538,"t":"Southshore","lv":38,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Loremaster Dibbs in Southshore.","desc":"‹name›. If you don't mind a long journey then I have a task for you, to again help Stormwind fill its library.\nThe old kingdom of Alterac fell after the great war, and it had a large collection of books. It's a tragedy that the city is ruined, but even more tragic is all of their knowledge lost! We must recover what we can.\nSouthshore is the closest town to the Ruins of Alterac. Go there and speak with Loremaster Dibbs. He can direct you to the ruins, and to what books may be found there.","rew":"Experience: 700\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Ah yes, I remember Milton. A bookworm, no doubt. Bless him.\nAnd he's right. The Ruins of Alterac still hold stores of knowledge in danger of being lost!\nOgres now dwell in Alterac, and they don't care much for higher learning.\nStormwind City Hillsbrad Foothills","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":77.1,"y":30.2,"n":"Milton Sheaf","s":1},{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":50.6,"y":57.1,"n":"Loremaster Dibbs","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"618":{"id":618,"t":"Facing Negolash","lv":50,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 35 instead of 40.","obj":"Bring 10 Barbecued Buzzard Wings and 5 bottles of Junglevine Wine to Captain Smotts' Lifeboat.\nKill Negolash, and bring Smotts' Cutlass to Captain Smotts in Stranglethorn.\nSmotts' Cutlass Negolash","desc":"Negolash is a hungry giant.\nWhen the giants destroyed our ship, Negolash went straight for my kitchen. He wasn't hungry for crew like the other giants. Negolash wanted wine...and my Barbecued Buzzard Wings. They're my specialty, and I had to go all the way to the Badlands for the recipe!\nIf you want to lure the giant, then get some wine and a heap of buzzard wings. Put them in our old lifeboat, southeast of here along the coast. When Negolash smells all that food, he'll come for sure!","rew":"You will receive:\nSmotts' Compass\nExperience: 7,100\n+200 reputation with Booty Bay\n-1,000 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"Did you get my cutlass, ‹name›?","done":"You got my cutlass from Negolash! I can't believe my fortune, ‹name›! Meeting you has turned my luck to the better, make no mistake there!\nThank you! And if I ever get a new ship and you're looking to sail the seas, you would be my honored guest.\nStranglethorn Vale Open the zone on the world map Level 50 , requires level 35 Difficulty 35 46 48 53 60 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Elite Shareable Yes Quest ID 618\nThe chain\n4 quests from level 50 to 52, 9,920 XP in all.\n1 [ 50 ] The Monogrammed Sash\nReturn the Monogrammed Sash to its owner.\nMonogrammed Sash\n2,350 XP\n2 [ 50 ] The Captain's Cutlass\nSpeak with Sprogger.\n470 XP\n3 [ 50 ] Facing Negolash this quest\nBring 10 Barbecued Buzzard Wings and 5 bottles of Junglevine Wine to Captain Smotts' Lifeboat. Kill Negolash, and bring Smotts' Cutlass to Captain Smotts in Stranglethorn.\n7,100 XP\n4 [ 52 ] Enticing Negolash\nRuined Lifeboat Stranglethorn Vale","cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8058":{"id":8058,"t":"Paragons of Power: The Vindicator's Armguards","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 6,500, 1.02 times as much.","obj":"Bring Jin'rokh the Breaker a Primal Hakkari Armsplint. You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Friendly with the Zandalar Tribe.\nJin'rokh the Breaker is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\nPrimal Hakkari Armsplint\nReach 3000 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","desc":"Vengeance is power. The Zandalar vindicator is such power. The tribe has many enemies. The vindicator exacts retribution on them. No crime against us is unpunished. The vindicator delivers this punishment. Our enemies fear our vengeance. They should. They forever will.\nBecome one of our vindicators. Seek the Paragons of Power inside Zul'Gurub. Slay the minions of Hakkar and claim vengeance in the tribe's name. You will be rewarded.","rew":"You will receive:\nZandalar Vindicator's Armguards\nExperience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Have you brought the Paragons of Power? Has vengeance been claimed in the name of the Zandalar?","done":"You have wrought much vengeance today. You have taken on the visage of the vindicator. You have brought the Blood God's minions to their knees.\nTake this. It will fuel your vengeance for the future. You are a friend to the Zandalar now.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":14.4,"n":"Jin'rokh the Breaker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"1418":{"id":1418,"t":"Neeka Bloodscar","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Neeka Bloodscar.","desc":"The Badlands is harsh and lies close to the Alliance-held land of Loch Modan, so communication between Stonard and the Badlands outpost of Kargath is often cut.\nProve yourself, ‹name›. Travel to the Badlands and speak with Neeka Bloodscar, head scout of the Kargath outpost. Speak with her, and then send her report back to me.","rew":"Experience: 1,350\n+50 reputation with Orgrimmar","done":"Helgrum wants a report, eh? I sent an outrunner to Stonard not three days past. Did he fail his mission? If Stonard does not have my report, then it appears he did fail.\nLet's hope the next runner I send has more skill, or more luck.\nSwamp of Sorrows Badlands","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":47.7,"y":55.2,"n":"Helgrum the Swift","s":1},{"z":"Badlands","x":6.5,"y":47.2,"n":"Neeka Bloodscar","e":1}],"cats":["swamp-of-sorrows"]},"698":{"id":698,"t":"Lack of Surplus","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 8 Unprepared Sawtooth Flanks to Tok'Kar in Swamp of Sorrows.\n8 Unprepared Sawtooth Flank Sawtooth Crocolisk 25 % , Sawtooth Snapper 25 %","desc":"I'm working on getting some supplies together for our outpost near the beach to the east--Tok'kar does what he can, but between shifts of guard duty and cooking for his soldiers there's not much time left in the day.\nThey do enjoy cooking up some sawtooth meat when they can, but I haven't had time to get them another shipment. Would you mind helping them out?\nThe young sawtooths aren't as tasty as the older ones, so stay clear of those; give them a year or two to get to full size.","rew":"Experience: 3,150\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Lok'tar, ‹class›. Traveling through the swamps isn't a risk taken lightly. You're brave to test your mettle here.","done":"Ah! Wonderful. Fresh meat for the fire tonight. Thank you, ‹name›.\nYou've helped make the coming nights more tolerable. The fire burns bright, and our stomachs will be full.\nIts a pleasant surprise to have you bring us a shipment; Dar's not the most attractive orc anyone's laid eyes upon, but at least his attitude reeks far less than his smell.","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":44.7,"y":57.2,"n":"Dar","s":1},{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":81.3,"y":81,"n":"Tok'Kar","e":1}],"cats":["swamp-of-sorrows"]},"458":{"id":458,"t":"The Woodland Protector","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Mining for Dummies, Wild Harvest, Pelt Collecting for Beginners. Partly read from what the game server sent.","obj":"Seek out the dryad known as Tarindrella.","desc":"Thank goodness you are here, ‹class›. Strange news has traveled to me through the whisperings of the forest spirits.\nThe mysterious woodland protector, Tarindrella, has returned to Shadowglen. The dryad's presence has not been felt in the forests of Kalimdor in years. Something is surely amiss if she has journeyed back to this land.\nSeek out Tarindrella and see what business she tends to in our grove. One of the Sentinels reported seeing her to the southwest of Aldrassil.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMining for Dummies Wild Harvest Pelt Collecting for Beginners\nNew in Forever: Mining for Dummies, Wild Harvest, Pelt Collecting for Beginners.\nExperience: 40\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","done":"I see you found me, young ‹race›. Melithar is a wise druid to have sent you.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":59.9,"y":42.5,"n":"Melithar Staghelm","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":57.8,"y":45.2,"n":"Tarindrella","e":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"938":{"id":938,"t":"Mist","lv":12,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Escort Mist to Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak at the moon well near the Oracle Tree.","desc":"The sabercat's fur is a distinctive gray color, blending into the surrounding forest. As she lays there, you observe that she is badly wounded, with deep lacerations across her back and stomach.\nShe raises her head and gazes at you, bright intelligence shining in blue eyes. She seems to wish to follow you.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCord Bracers Crag Buckler Scout's Cloak\nExperience: 900\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Mist... It was my fault! The witches caught me off guard... I should not have let them take you...","done":"Oh, thank you, ‹name›! I feared I would never see Mist again, knowing only her death in my heart, never to be united with my faithful companion. I owe you more than you can know, and you have my eternal gratitude.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":31.5,"y":31.6,"n":"Mist","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":38.3,"y":34.4,"n":"Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak","e":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"858":{"id":858,"t":"Ignition","lv":18,"min":13,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Get the Ignition Key and bring it to Wizzlecrank.\nIgnition Key Supervisor Lugwizzle","desc":"I don't suppose Sputtervalve sent you? I'm in a bind here. I hopped in without realizing that I need a key to unlock the shredder's movement column. One of the other shredder operators asked me if everything was okay, and I panicked! Instead of telling him that I was missing my key, I told him there was some sort of mechanical problem.\nWe need to get out of here on the double! Go up to the control room at the top of the derrick, the supervisor should have a key for this shredder.\nHelp me out here!","rew":"Experience: 1,350\n+100 reputation with Ratchet","back":"Quick, we need to get out of here before someone gets suspicious!","done":"Yep, this looks like the right key. Let me just make sure I know how to work this thing...\nHmm... rotation control... This regulates speed and stability... fine arm movement control. Just look at this! I can't believe the Venture Company could design something this much better than ours. I've got to get this back to Ratchet!","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":56.5,"y":7.5,"n":"Wizzlecrank's Shredder","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"2938":{"id":2938,"t":"Venom to the Undercity","lv":55,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Faranell's Parcel to Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity.\nFaranell's Parcel\nProvided: Faranell's Parcel","desc":"The venom you gathered from the Witherbark's spider god is quite a find! I've been able to kill nearly two dozen rabbits with just a drop of the stuff. Granted, some of those rabbits were very young and small enough to fit in the palm of one's hand so I'm certain their resistance to toxins was low, but it can't be denied that this poison is powerful!\nI'd like a sample sent to my superior, Apothecary Faranell in the Apothecarium of the Undercity. I am positive he would want to test this himself.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nRoyal Highmark Vestments Honorguard Chestpiece Aegis of Battle\nMoney: 2 50 2 gold, 50 silver, 0 copper Experience: 8,450\n+200 reputation with Undercity","back":"Word was sent of your coming, ‹name›. You have a parcel for me?","done":"Ah, very good. Lydon mentioned the poison in this parcel is the most potent he has come in contact with, and is busy working on new applications with it.\nWith luck, we will find many.\nThank you, ‹name›. Your service to the Royal Apothecary Society is undeniable.\nHillsbrad Foothills Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":61.4,"y":19.1,"n":"Apothecary Lydon","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":48.8,"y":69.3,"n":"Master Apothecary Faranell","e":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"378":{"id":378,"t":"The Fury Runs Deep","lv":27,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Magistrate's Pantaloons. Reported by players.","obj":"Motley Garmason wants Kam Deepfury's head brought to him at Dun Modr.\nHead of Deepfury Kam Deepfury","desc":"You have proven your loyalty to King Magni, ‹class›. And your hatred for the Dark Iron scum is as great as my own.\nThere is a task I wish to complete myself but I am bound by honor to stay with Longbraid. But Roggo has gathered intelligence that proves Kam Deepfury was a conspirator in the attack on the Thandol Span. It was by Deepfury's planning that Longbraid lost his kin.\nDeepfury is being held for political reasons in the Stormwind Stockade. I want him dead, ‹name›. For Longbraid! Bring me his head!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBelt of Vindication Headbasher Magistrate's Pantaloons\nNew in Forever: Magistrate's Pantaloons.\nExperience: 2,750\n+150 reputation with Ironforge","back":"I won't let foolish Human bureaucracy interfere with Dwarven matters, ‹name›. Kam Deepfury is a proven conspirator in the Thandol Span attack. King Magni's good people lost their lives because of Deepfury's deceit. The Humans might be content to let Deepfury rot in The Stockade but I will not sleep soundly at night until Deepfury is slain.","done":"So Kam Deepfury finally got to feel what it is like to be on the receiving end of Death? Good. Serves the cowardly Dark Iron scum right. You have done well, ‹class›. The victims of the Thandol Span attack were but mere victims in a world torn with war and unrest. Their families will have the peace of knowing Deepfury got the punishment he deserved. Longbraid's brother's death has been avenged.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":49.7,"y":18.2,"n":"Motley Garmason","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-stockade"]},"1178":{"id":1178,"t":"Goblin Sponsorship","lv":37,"min":29,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Gazlowe in Ratchet.","desc":"Our racing team is the pride of goblins everywhere. You'd be surprised at some of the people who contribute in one way or another to our team.\nYou know Gazlowe? He tracks down parts from around the world for us. He even came down to work on one of our rigs once!\nA few weeks ago, he said he'd send us a new prototype fuel regulator but it hasn't come yet. He's usually very prompt... Maybe you wouldn't mind going to Ratchet to ask him about it? I wouldn't be so pushy, but the gnomes are gaining on us!","rew":"Experience: 700\n+25 reputation with Ratchet","done":"Pozzik sent you, huh? You know, Pozzik was one of the most respected tinkerers in Undermine before he retired to start working on the racers.\nThe first thing he did when he joined the team was develop the two engine model racers. Could be that the businesses will suffer without him working with the Tinkers' Union, but who cares, right? There's nothing like the races!\nThousand Needles The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":80.2,"y":75.9,"n":"Pozzik","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.7,"y":36.2,"n":"Gazlowe","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"7818":{"id":7818,"t":"A Donation of Runecloth","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"60 Runecloth Stormwind Royal Guard , Honor Guard , Skullsplitter Speaker in Zul'Gurub , General Marcus Jonathan 85.7 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Undercity","back":"‹name›, you've been a tremendous contributor to our cloth drive. As we work hard to replenish our reserves, one form of cloth remains critically low - runecloth. We are in absolutely dire need of runecloth, and we hope that you will be able to help us as you have in the past.\nIf you are willing, please bring me what runecloth you can spare. We'll initially accept a single donation of sixty, and then we'll go from there.","done":"Fantastic - these will go right to use, I assure you. Thank you again for your assistance! We'd certainly be lost without you.\nWith all the donations you've made, I would certainly process any additional runecloth donations you care to make in the future. Just be sure to check in with me, and I'll personally make sure that your good deeds won't go unrecognized!","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":71.7,"y":29.2,"n":"Ralston Farnsley","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["undercity"]},"1738":{"id":1738,"t":"Heartswood","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve the Heartswood from Ashenvale and bring it to Gakin the Darkbinder in the Mage Quarter of Stormwind.\nHeartswood Dark Strand Excavator , Heartswood","desc":"In preparation for your coming, I used my sight to look over the world and through the mists of time. I have found what it is you seek.\nIn the War of the Ancients, two lovers fell together in battle. Where they took their last breaths, a tree known as the heartswood grew, a symbol of their undying love.\nThat should be enough to tempt a succubus. You will find it in the ruins of Ordil'Aran in the northwestern part of the forest of Ashenvale.","rew":"Experience: 1,550","back":"Was your search a success, ‹name›?","done":"Yes, I can tell this will do nicely, let me just work with it for a moment...\nTakar is a resourceful fellow to have around, isn't he? If only I could persuade him to move back to civilization.\nThe Barrens Stormwind City Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":49.3,"y":57.1,"n":"Takar the Seer","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":39.2,"y":85.2,"n":"Gakin the Darkbinder","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1498":{"id":1498,"t":"Path of Defense","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 5 Singed Scales to Uzzek at Far Watch Post in the Barrens.\n5 Singed Scale Lightning Hide 80 % , Thunder Lizard 80 %","desc":"As a warrior, one of our most crucial tasks is... protection. We are the shield of the Horde, and we keep our weaker brethren safe. If you are to join in our ranks, then you must prove your mettle to me.\nGo to Thunder Ridge in Durotar, where live the lightning hides and thunder lizards. Hunt the beasts! Show me you are tougher than they! Brave their assaults and bring me a stack of their singed scales as proof.\nDo this, and then I will teach you.","back":"Do you have the scales, ‹name›? Unless you can withstand the attacks of the thunder lizards, you will not benefit from my instruction.","done":"Ah. I see you have defeated the thunder lizards, which proves you are tough. Now I will show you how tough skin and shrewd movements can combine to form an impenetrable wall of defense.\nLearn your lesson well, ‹name›. And be ready for future instruction.\nThe Barrens Durotar","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":61.4,"y":21.1,"n":"Uzzek","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"1818":{"id":1818,"t":"Speak with Dillinger","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Deathguard Dillinger in Brill.","desc":"I was told Deathguard Dillinger has a job for someone like you. If you're willing to show your value to the Dark Lady's forces, then report to Dillinger immediately.\nDeathguard Dillinger's post is on the west end of Brill, near the graveyard.","rew":"Experience: 85","done":"You're here for a mission? Good. I have an important one, and one that will test your skill in combat... and your resolve in the defense of the Forsaken.\nTirisfal Glades Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.9,"y":52.5,"n":"Austil de Mon","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":58.2,"y":51.4,"n":"Deathguard Dillinger","e":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":47.4,"y":17.3,"n":"Baltus Fowler","s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"5098":{"id":5098,"t":"All Along the Watchtowers","lv":56,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Using the Beacon Torch, mark each tower in Andorhal; you will need to stand in the doorway of the tower to successfully mark it.\nOnce all four towers are marked, return the Beacon Torch to High Executor Derrington at the Bulwark, Western Plaguelands.\nTower One marked\nTower Two marked\nTower Three marked\nTower Four marked\nProvided: Beacon Torch","desc":"Through the use of a magical device known as a beacon torch, we can mark targets of our choosing for future actions by our troops. To that end, we think the Scourge are using Andorhal's watchtowers as a means to control their troop movements.\nYour mission: breach Andorhal's defenses to plant beacons at all four watchtowers. You'll need to be in the doorway of each tower to plant the beacon; it will then proceed to mark the tower. There are only five charges on the beacon torch, so use them wisely!","rew":"Money: 85 0 gold, 85 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,800\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Once the towers are marked, they'll become top priority targets for our attack on Andorhal. I suspect that once we neutralize the towers, the main threat of Andorhal will emerge. From that point on, we'll have a straight-up fight for control of the city!\nYou're back to report success, yes? Don't forget the beacon torch as well; we must maintain control of our materiel.","done":"My priests are reporting that our beacon trackers are picking up extremely strong signals on all four towers! Dare I say it, but I believe you've executed another mission with complete and total success! Well played once again, ‹name›!\nWith the towers marked, our preparations for the attack are now in place. The time has come to take the fight to the Scourge!\nTirisfal Glades Western Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83.1,"y":68.9,"n":"High Executor Derrington","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"138":{"id":138,"t":"Captain Sander's Hidden Treasure","lv":16,"min":10,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the old barrel near the ruined chimney and search it for your next clue.\nProvided: A Clue to Sander's Treasure","desc":"The clue to the treasure reads: Good work, matey! Now ye need to head due east. East up the bluffs, east to the road. Look for the ol' chimney ruins near the side of the road. There you'll find an old barrel with your next clue.","rew":"Experience: 575","done":"Good work, treasure hunter!","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":25.9,"y":47.8,"n":"Captain's Footlocker","s":1},{"z":"Westfall","x":40.5,"y":47.8,"n":"Broken Barrel","e":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"93738":{"id":93738,"t":"The broken construct","lv":9,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Report back to Ayessa Dawnsinger in Valanaar.","desc":"Brightwish, eh? So the High Order wanted to remove these components for some reason. But why though?\nThe High Order has always been meddlesome, constantly wanting to experiment with the wind spirits' magic. They are too bold by a mile, and we've strictly forbade them from meddling with knowledge under Windshaper purview, but lately they've been testing our patience.\nI think you should report what you've learned back to Ayessa Dawnsinger. She can instruct you further on what to do.","done":"Very interesting, so it was the High Order that was responsible for the construct breaking down?\nI know Belathaan. He's Valennia Stormfist's cousin and his mother was actually a Windshaper. It's disappointing that he was involved in this.\nI need to reflect on this for a moment.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":59,"y":73,"n":"Riaani Nightwind","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":59,"y":79.6,"n":"Ayessa Dawnsinger","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"92698":{"id":92698,"t":"What is my purpose","lv":9,"min":5,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Aamelia Windfield about the Malfunctioning Cyclone Construct.","desc":"<You lean in close to try and hear the words coming from beneath the giant construct's armor plates.>\n...Function error...\n...Question...\n...What is....\n...Function...\n<These fragmented words and phrases seem to just repeat. Maybe someone nearby knows more about this construct?>","done":"The construct? It's been wandering around the fields for decades. Since the wind elementals left us, I think. Alvarion suspected that it used to haul harvests to market, or maybe tend to livestock back before this was an orchard. That could have been a thousand years ago though.\nIn the old days, the Windshapers used to maintain these constructs. We've talked about petitioning them to come and take a look at it, but it's never been a pressing concern to us. Mostly we just ignore it these days.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":48.8,"y":78.4,"n":"Malfunctioning Cyclone Construct","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":46.6,"y":81.8,"n":"Aamelia Windfield","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]}});